3. Plans and machine licenses

Plans are described at https://orcraft.app/pricing/. A remote endpoint
machine is licensed to one account or team at a time, takes one slot
when a signed-in controller activates it, and gives the slot back when
its license is revoked. A machine license lasts a limited time and is
renewed by a signed-in controller. We may refuse or revoke activations
that exceed a plan or circumvent the counting. A controller running
tests on its own computer needs no account and no slot.

Machine licenses are ordinarily renewed through the Orcraft account and
licensing service. If GM Core Ltd. permanently discontinues that
service, GM Core Ltd. shall make available, before the planned
discontinuation, a final version of the Software allowing customers
holding valid licenses at the time of discontinuation to continue
operating their existing licensed installations without periodic online
license renewal. The final version shall preserve the material
functionality available to the customer immediately before
discontinuation, subject to applicable law, third-party intellectual
property rights, and technical limitations inherent in the Software.
This undertaking does not entitle customers to additional machine
licenses, future updates, new functionality, maintenance, or technical
support following discontinuation. GM Core Ltd. shall provide reasonable
advance notice of planned discontinuation where practicable. In
connection with any sale or transfer of the Orcraft product line or
substantially all assets relating to the Software, GM Core Ltd. shall
require the acquiring entity to expressly assume the continuity
obligations applicable to existing customers, to the extent such
assumption is within GM Core Ltd.'s contractual control. Nothing in this
provision overrides mandatory applicable law, including insolvency
legislation.

4. Open source components

The Software includes open source libraries under their own licenses,
listed with the package. Nothing in this agreement limits the rights
those licenses give you in those libraries. The controller's user
interface is built with Qt through PySide6, used under the GNU Lesser
General Public License, version 3. Qt is installed beside the Software
as a separate, unmodified library, so you may replace it with your own
build of the same release.

In the event of any conflict between this Agreement and the terms of an
applicable third-party open-source license, the rights granted under
that open-source license shall prevail with respect to the relevant
component. Nothing in this Agreement shall prevent the exercise of
rights that cannot lawfully be restricted under the applicable open-
source license.

5. Your tests and data

Your test suites, systems under test, test results, logs, and other
content generated through your testing activities remain yours. GM Core
Ltd. does not acquire ownership rights in that content. The Software is
designed so that the controller and endpoint application exchange
testing information within your own network, without transmitting test
suites, results, or logs to GM Core Ltd. through the ordinary operation
of the Software. Account information, licensing identifiers, technical
metadata, and information voluntarily submitted through customer support
may be processed separately, as described in the Privacy Policy. You
remain responsible for your testing activities, the content you create,
and the systems on which you perform tests.

