9. Termination

You may stop using the Software at any time by uninstalling it. GM Core
Ltd. may suspend or terminate your access to the Software and related
account services in the event of a material breach of this Agreement.
Where the breach is capable of remedy, GM Core Ltd. shall provide
written notice specifying the breach and allow fourteen (14) days from
receipt of such notice for you to remedy it. Notwithstanding the
foregoing, GM Core Ltd. may immediately suspend access where reasonably
necessary to address security threats, unauthorized use, deliberate
circumvention of licensing mechanisms, violations of applicable law, or
other serious circumstances requiring immediate intervention. GM Core
Ltd. may terminate the Agreement immediately where a material breach is
incapable of remedy or where an applicable law requires termination. GM
Core Ltd. shall exercise its contractual suspension and termination
rights reasonably and in good faith. Corresponding termination
provisions in the Terms of Use shall be interpreted consistently with
this section.

Upon termination, you shall cease using the Software and discontinue any
use of related machine licenses, except as otherwise required by
mandatory law. Suspension or termination shall not affect rights or
obligations accrued before termination. Sections 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 and
10, together with the continuity undertaking in Section 3 and any other
provisions intended by their nature to survive termination, shall remain
effective to the extent applicable.

